			<div class="content" id="post-content-4132822">
									

<p>Reasons for my downvote:</p>
<ul>
<li>The description is way more convoluted than it needs to be.</li>
<li>I'm not a scientist, but the &quot;5000% increase in nuclear radiation&quot; sets off serious realism red flags for me. <a href="https://jciv.iidj.net/map/">Cursory research</a> indicates that 5000% of the average background radiation in Ibaraki would be about 0.7 millirems, max. You're exposed to 40 millirems at the dentist. Furthermore, a &quot;10-cm-wide area&quot; would be two-dimensional, and even a 10cm<sup>2</sup> area would be ridiculously hard to detect within a whole country in the 13 seconds it manifested.</li>
<li>The [DATA EXPUNGED] noodle incident is really cliche.</li>
<li>The 682 reference is really, <em>really</em> cliche.</li>
</ul>
<p>Overall, it's a interesting enough idea, but the execution could use more work.</p>

